          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Somites differentiate into three components. Which component gives rise to the v</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Somites differentiate into three components. Which component gives rise to the vertebral bodies, arches, and ribs?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Myotome</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. The myotome gives rise to the skeletal muscles of the trunk, with each segment corresponding to one spinal nerve level.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Dermatome</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. The dermatome forms the dermis of the back and carries sensory innervation from one spinal nerve.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Septum transversum</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. The septum transversum arises from the lateral plate mesoderm and becomes the central tendon of the diaphragm, not part of the vertebral column.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Sclerotome</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct! The sclerotome, the ventromedial portion of the somite, condenses around the notochord to form the vertebral bodies, arches, intervertebral discs, and ribs.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Each somite has three derivatives: sclerotome (vertebral bodies, arches, discs, ribs), myotome (trunk skeletal muscles), and dermatome (dermis of the back)."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! The sclerotome forms the axial skeleton. Remember: sclerotome → vertebrae and ribs; myotome → trunk muscles; dermatome → back dermis."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
